     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day is the usual practical ceiling. A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 mg to 1000 mg per dose. At this level the risks include severe GI intolerance and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **1700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg to 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, the more typical range\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and add a note about the rationale. I'll enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably still flag it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
